.TH SAPHIRA-PROFILES 5 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
saphira-profiles \- install profile format for saphira-bootstrap
.SH DESCRIPTION
An install profile declares
.B top-level package intentions
for one kind of Saphira system. Profiles are consumed by
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8),
which installs them with the package manager into an empty target
directory. Image creation
.RB ( saphira-image )
and disk installation
.RB ( saphira-install )
assemble their root filesystems from the same profiles through the
same code path, so a profile that builds a working image always
installs a working system.
.SS Format
One entry per line. Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
are ignored. Any other line is either a package name or a profile
include:
.TP
.I package
A package name to install: letters, digits, dot, underscore, plus
and hyphen only.
.TP
.IB @ name
Include the profile called
.IR name :
its entries are expanded in place, recursively, with reference-cycle
detection. The historical
.IB @akadata-stage4- name
spelling includes the profile called
.IR name .
.PP
Duplicate packages across includes are installed once.
.SS The profile invariant
A profile lists
.B only
explicit intentions. It must never enumerate resolved dependencies:
dependency closure belongs to APK metadata
.RB ( depends ),
not to the image definition. A profile that duplicates the package
database rots the moment any dependency changes; a profile of
intentions stays correct because the resolver re-proves it on every
install. Validate a profile by resolving it against the repository
index and proving every transitive dependency is satisfiable \-
before touching image assembly.
.SH PROFILES
.TP
.B base
Minimal bootable skeleton: ABI marker, layout, shell and core tools.
.TP
.B network
Base plus network diagnostics and firewalling.
.TP
.B server
Network plus the hosted-service stack.
.TP
.B build
Server plus compilers and packaging tools.
.TP
.B virtualisation-host
First image-architecture profile: a boring x86-64 systemd
virtualisation host.
.RS
.PP
.nf
saphira-base
saphira-kernel
systemd
saphira-virtualisation
saphira-network-host
openssh
.fi
.PP
.BR saphira-base ,
.BR saphira-virtualisation
and
.B saphira-network-host
are metapackages: they carry no payload and exist only to give a
name, owned by APK metadata, to each dependency stack. The kernel
and the init system are named here on purpose \-
.B saphira-base
stays kernel-agnostic and init-neutral so later profiles (for
example an OpenRC image) can reuse it unchanged.
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/saphira/profiles/
Profile directory read by
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8)
(overridable with
.BR SAPHIRA_PROFILE_ROOT ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR saphira-bootstrap (8)
